Specifications and templates
----------------------------

Submodel templates (src/aas_editor/submodel_templates/)
    The folder holds submodel templates and their specification documents as
    published by the IDTA in https://github.com/admin-shell-io/submodel-templates.
    That repository states the license Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
    International (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.
    The copyright in each template remains with the IDTA and the authors named
    in the template. The files are included to be opened and used as
    templates by the editor. Each template folder has its own README.md and
    specification document, which name its version and origin.

AAS metamodel schema (aas_test_engines/data/file/3.0.yml)
    A JSON schema of the metamodel of the Asset Administration Shell, in YAML.
    The repository does not record where the file came from. The metamodel
    specification is published by the IDTA and Plattform Industrie 4.0 in
    https://github.com/admin-shell-io/aas-specs-metamodel, which states the
    license CC BY 4.0.

Measurement units
    The specification of measurement units is published in
    https://github.com/admin-shell-io/aas-specs-measurement-units, which
    states the license CC BY 4.0.

Dictionaries (ECLASS, IEC Common Data Dictionary, and others)
    The software does not ship a global dictionary as such. The submodel
    templates above may refer to dictionary entries or hold some, and a
    package that a user opens, or a dictionary that a user loads or imports,
    may contain such content. The license of that content stays with its
    owner, and this project grants no rights over it. The user is responsible
    for the license of the dictionaries and data that the user loads.


Software included in the repository
-----------------------------------

aas-test-engines (aas_test_engines/ and the installed package)
    The installed package states the Apache License 2.0,
    https://github.com/admin-shell-io/aas-test-engines. The folder
    aas_test_engines/ holds data files that the editor ships with the
    stand-alone build: the schema above, and an HTML template that the
    installed package also has. The folder has no license file of its own.

Breeze stylesheets (src/aas_editor/themes/dark.qss and light.qss)
    MIT License. The headers of both files name Colin Duquesnoy and Alex Huszagh
    as the authors, and hold the license text. The stylesheets are based on the
    Breeze color scheme, and are not affiliated with KDE. The generated
    breeze_resources.py holds the compiled resources of the theme folders. The
    other files in src/aas_editor/themes/, such as grey.qss and default.qss,
    state no license of their own.

Tabler Icons (src/aas_editor/icons/tabler/)
    Version 3.50.0 of https://github.com/tabler/tabler-icons, the outline
    style. The 53 SVG files are unmodified copies, and are the icons of
    actions in the toolbars, menus and trees. MIT License, "Copyright (c)
    2020-2026 Paweł Kuna". The license text is in the file LICENSE of that
    folder, and is the text of the same release. The editor draws the files
    in a color of the theme, and does not change them.

Icons of the kinds of AAS elements (src/aas_editor/icons/kinds/)
    The 24 SVG files that mark the kinds of elements in the trees (shell,
    submodel, concept description, the elements, and the parts such as
    qualifier and reference) are the own work of this project, drawn for it in
    2026, and are under its license, the GNU General Public License, version
    3. Each is a shape for the family of the kind, with one or two letters for
    the kind. The shapes and the letters were drawn from scratch on a grid of
    16 by 16 pixels with a stroke of 1.33. The letters are skeletons of lines
    that were made for these files, and are written as paths, so no font is
    needed and none is embedded. No file of another set of icons, and no
    outline of a font, was copied, traced or used as a model. They carry no
    third-party license and need no attribution.

Inter (src/aas_editor/fonts/)
    The font of the user interface. Inter is by The Inter Project Authors
    (https://github.com/rsms/inter), and the font file states "Copyright 2016
    The Inter Project Authors". SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The font
    has no Reserved Font Name. The file Inter-Variable.ttf is the variable
    font, version "4.001;git-66647c0bb" (release 4.1 of the project), copied
    unmodified from the Google Fonts repository
    (https://github.com/google/fonts, folder ofl/inter, commit e1d6480) under
    the name Inter[opsz,wght].ttf, and renamed only to avoid brackets in a
